Package: tower
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), procps
Recommends: systemd, tmux
Suggests: nodejs
Homepage: https://github.com/imanimen/tower
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Description: control tower for your Claude Code agents
 Tower pins Claude Code to a country (the fence), isolates network faults
 (the weather), watches plan usage, and monitors every running Claude agent.
 .
 One daemon owns all the logic and state; the front-ends are thin. On Linux
 the front-end is the curses terminal dashboard, "tower" — the macOS menu-bar
 app has no Linux counterpart.
 .
 The guard is fail-closed: a Claude request is allowed only when Tower has
 *confirmed* you are inside the target country and that there is a usable
 network path to Anthropic. Anything uncertain is held and answered 503, which
 Claude Code shows as its own "Retrying" spinner, so a blocked request is
 pending rather than failed and resumes on its own.
 .
 Routing is installed by editing the "env" block of ~/.claude/settings.json
 only — never a shell alias — and it is removed again on every clean exit.
